  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Shelter Services and Non-food Items to Vulnerable Ethiopian Returnee</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Overall, Ethiopians returnees require a range of basic and specialized forms of assistance. All returnees require immediate post-arrival assistance, including essential non-food items (NFIs) and short-term shelter in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia. Most returnees can travel to their home communities shortly after receiving this basic assistance, but the screening procedures of the Government of Ethiopia, IOM and other actors routinely identify migrants who need further assistance, which if not provided, would exacerbate vulnerabilities to threats or increase risks to the lives of migrants. Such cases require appropriate shelter services for extended periods of time. Furthermore, despite the recent peace treaty and cessation of hostilities, many Tigrayan returnees are unable to return to devastated communities or reunify with family. The proposed project aims to provide humanitarian assistance to vulnerable Ethiopian returnee migrants through the provision of shelter services and NFIs upon arrival back to Ethiopia, to support their return to their home communities, and to create awareness among Ethiopians in their communities of origin so that make informed migration decisions and do not pursue irregular ways to migrate.</narrative>
  </description>
